<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Interpretation: the slow half of listening, which works out what a scored sound turns
  out to be. The listening (abilities/listening/listening.scx) invokes it
  as its long-lived child "interpretation" and hands it each scored sound.

    initializing -> Interpretation {
      Idle -bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output-> Working {
        DetectingVoice -> Idle | HandingOff | ClassifyingSound
                        | IdentifyingVoiceDirect | HearingSpeech
        HearingSpeech -scored sound-> FeedingSpeech
        FeedingSpeech -> HearingSpeech | SpeechEnded
        SpeechEnded -> DiarizingVoice | DecodingSpeech | Idle
        ClassifyingSound -> HandingOff | Idle
        DiarizingVoice -> IdentifyingVoice | DecodingSpeech.Diarized | HandingOff
        IdentifyingVoiceDirect -> HearingSpeech
        IdentifyingVoice -> HandingOff
        DecodingSpeech { Detected, Diarized } -> IdentifyingVoice | HandingOff
        HandingOff -> Idle }
      Idle -bot.ability.speaking.efference {audio}-> Working.DetectingOwnVoice
        -> IdentifyingOwnVoice -> Idle
      Working -bot.ability.listening.stage.failed-> Idle }

  Configuration (as <data>): the voice activity
  classifier is required, so voice detection always runs;
  sound_classification (labelled from the sound's kind, no model), speech_decoding,
  voice_diarization and voice_identification say which optional stages are
  configured, product_threshold_db is 3 dB, stage_timeout_ms is 30 s, the
  stage operation timeout, and recognize_timeout_ms 2 s (decision D177).
  floppy's bot configures voice
  detection, sound classification and speech decoding (the phase 6 plan:
  speech is decoded in listening), with voice diarization and voice
  identification, so decoded speech says who spoke. A negative
  product_threshold_db and a recognize_timeout_ms that is not positive are
  refused: initializing ends in the final state degraded, and the
  listening degrades.

  Input: bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output {sound, parent,
  perceived_level_db, producing} (sensitivity's output) from the
  listening. The bot's own voice arriving as predicted (producing, with a
  perceived_level_db below product_threshold_db) is not interpreted: Idle
  and HearingSpeech take it and do nothing, so it neither opens an
  utterance nor joins the open one, and a person's words heard while the
  bot speaks, or just after it, stay one utterance of their own (#30;
  mosfet.py's streaming hearing gates its predicted voice the same way,
  W3-11). Anything else heard while producing (another source, or the
  bot's own voice coming back wrong) is interpreted as usual, and the one
  comparison at HandingOff still decides whether it is a turn. Scored
  sounds that arrive while Working are held by
  <event:defer/> (scxml.rs namespaces/event) and taken, in order, by Idle
  and HearingSpeech: interpretation is serial, and
  the score was taken on arrival.

  Stages, each a child invoked from its state (leaving the state cancels
  it, SCXML 6.4) and bounded by its own stage timer:
  bot.ability.listening.stage.failed {stage, message: "Listening <stage>
  timed out."} sent to this session after stage_timeout_ms.

  * DetectingVoice and FeedingSpeech invoke abilities/voice_detection/voice_detection.scx:
    the sound normalized to PCM (a WAV
    container's PCM is written beside it as floppy-sound-<n>.pcm) and its
    voice spans (its ApplyData). With no voice: dropped when only
    speech decoding is configured, handed off as a silence observation
    when nothing else is, else classified. With voice: identified directly
    (voice identification without diarization), else the open-speech
    window opens (VAD Start).
  * HearingSpeech is the open-speech window: each scored sound goes to
    FeedingSpeech, still voiced it joins the utterance and the window stays
    open, and the first one without voice joins it and closes it
    (VAD End) in SpeechEnded. The utterance is the list open_frames (each
    frame's PCM reference and format), and the loudest frame is open_sensed. While the window is open and neither speech
    decoding nor diarization owns the product, each frame is streamed as
    an acoustic bot.ability.listening.speech.output (its PCM, its voice
    spans, and the identity direct identification found), when audible.
  * SpeechEnded joins the open speech into one utterance file with the
    speech service's append step when diarization or decoding will read
    it, then diarizes, else decodes, else returns to Idle. The utterance
    is a WAV container (floppy-utterance-<n>.wav) whenever its rate is
    known: floppy hands the decoder a file, and transcription APIs read a
    container, not raw PCM. Without a rate it stays raw PCM
    (floppy-utterance-<n>.pcm), and decoding then fails.
  * ClassifyingSound invokes abilities/sound_classification/sound_classification.scx: a
    labelled sound is non-speech and is handed off as its
    environment.sound envelope; an unlabelled one is dropped when speech decoding
    is configured, else handed off as a silence observation.
  * DiarizingVoice invokes abilities/voice_diarization/voice_diarization.scx on the
    utterance (its clipped segments are floppy-diarized-<n>-<index>).
  * IdentifyingVoiceDirect invokes abilities/voice_identification/voice_identification.scx on
    the opening voice span (clipped to floppy-voice-<n>.pcm); its one
    embedding becomes the window's source identity. IdentifyingVoice
    embeds each diarized segment. Exactly one embedding per segment. Both
    wait for their voices at most stage_timeout_ms + recognize_timeout_ms
    (decision D177): past that deadline, or with no opening embedding,
    identification completes as usual with nobody identified: the window
    opens with no source identity, or each segment is handed off with no embedding.
  * DecodingSpeech invokes abilities/speech_decoding/speech_decoding.scx (the speech
    service) on the utterance: decoding rewrites the observation into
    words. After diarization with voice identification configured, the
    words then go to IdentifyingVoice, which embeds the diarized segments
    of at least min_voice_seconds (1 s, mosfet.py's shortest new voice),
    or the longest when none is that long: decoded speech says who spoke
    (mosfet.py's streaming hearing does the same for each turn).
  * The bot's own voice is heard as any sound is: speaking's efference
    copy of a completed utterance carries the audio it commanded
    (bot.ability.speaking.efference {audio, media_type, sample_rate_hz,
    channels}), and while the bot's own voice is unknown and voice
    identification is configured, Idle takes it as the utterance:
    DetectingOwnVoice finds its voice (voice detection), and when at least
    min_voice_seconds of it is voiced, IdentifyingOwnVoice identifies that
    voice (direct identification of the span from its first voice to its
    last) and keeps it as own_voice. Serial work, so sounds wait behind
    it; a copy with too little voice, or whose voice cannot be identified
    in time, is logged (interpretation.unidentified) and the next copy is
    tried. A copy without audio, or once the voice is known, is nothing
    here.
  * HandingOff is the one comparison: a
    product whose perceived_level_db is null or at least
    product_threshold_db goes to the listening; a quieter one is dropped.
    The products: decoded
    speech as bot.ability.listening.speech.output with content the words
    and content_type text/plain (a sound with no sample rate fails), and,
    when its voices were identified, who spoke: each voice whose embedding
    is at least voice_similarity_threshold (0.50, mosfet.py's voice match)
    alike to own_voice is the bot's own and is no source; every other voice's
    embedding is one of its source_ids (at most 4, the first of alike
    ones), which the conversation identifies as a person. Only the voices
    that are not the bot's own become source_ids (mosfet.py). One speech product per diarized segment (its PCM, span,
    confidence, and, after identification, its embedding as its source
    identity); a silence observation as a speech product of the sound's
    PCM; a labelled sound, or a sound that is not PCM, as
    bot.ability.cognition.input {stimulus} whose stimulus is the
    environment.sound envelope (source "listening", the ability it hands
    off for), for the cognition.

  Participants (producers stamp, transformers copy): every scored sound taken adds the
  participants stamped on it to active_participants, their ordered union
  (each {ref, role} once, at most 32), cleared with the open speech; every
  speech product carries them, and the labelled-sound handoff carries them
  as its participants. The interpretation never works out who someone is;
  it only carries what the device stamped.

  Files are written in the directory of the sound's audio reference, the
  directory the run grants the speech service.

  Failure: a stage failure (its child's failure, an error, or its timer)
  answers the listening with bot.ability.listening.failed {stage, message}
  and returns to Idle; Idle clears the open
  speech.

  Readiness: on start it sends bot.ability.ready to the listening
  (decision D242); it offers nothing.

  Contracts: the events it takes reference abilities/schemas/ by
  event:schema (never inline). The stages' results are done.invoke
  <donedata>, which scxml.rs does not check, so their shape is checked by
  cond.

  Bindings: the speech service for the append step (no backend); the
  stages bind their own services.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="interpretation" initial="initializing">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- Configuration. -->
    <data id="product_threshold_db" expr="3.0"/>
    <data id="stage_timeout_ms" expr="30000"/>
    <!-- How much longer than a stage an utterance waits for its voices
         (2 s; decision D177). -->
    <data id="recognize_timeout_ms" expr="2000"/>
    <data id="sound_classifier" expr="true"/>
    <data id="speech_decoder" expr="true"/>
    <data id="diarizer" expr="true"/>
    <data id="voice_classifier" expr="true"/>
    <!-- Who spoke: the shortest segment embedded for decoded speech, the
         least cosine at which a voice is the bot's own (mosfet.py's voice
         match), and the bot's own voice once learned. -->
    <data id="min_voice_seconds" expr="1.0"/>
    <data id="voice_similarity_threshold" expr="0.5"/>
    <data id="own_voice" expr="null"/>
    <!-- Scored sounds waiting for the interpretation. -->
    <!-- The scored sound in hand, its stage, its directory, and a counter
         naming the files written for it. -->
    <data id="sensed" expr="null"/>
    <data id="stage" expr="null"/>
    <data id="media_dir" expr="''"/>
    <data id="serial" expr="0"/>
    <!-- The current frame's detection {sensed, voice_detection}, and what
         HandingOff hands off {kind, sensed, voice_detection, ...}. -->
    <data id="detection" expr="null"/>
    <data id="completion" expr="null"/>
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The open speech (the open utterance). -->
    <data id="open_frames" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="open_sensed" expr="null"/>
    <data id="active_source_ids" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="active_voice_embedding" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The ordered union of the participants stamped on the sound taken
         into the open utterance. -->
    <data id="active_participants" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="open_wav" expr="false"/>
    <data id="utterance" expr="null"/>
    <!-- HandingOff's working values. -->
    <data id="audible" expr="false"/>
    <data id="product" expr="null"/>
    <data id="mismatch" expr="null"/>
    <data id="channels" expr="1"/>
    <data id="segment" expr="null"/>
    <data id="index" expr="0"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="interpretation.js"/>

  <!-- The configuration's refusals, checked in order (decision D177). -->
  <state id="initializing">
    <transition cond="hasNegativeThreshold()" target="degraded">
      <log label="interpretation.degraded" expr="'product_threshold_db must not be negative'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition cond="hasNoRecognizeTimeout()" target="degraded">
      <log label="interpretation.degraded" expr="'recognize_timeout must be positive'"/>
    </transition>
    <transition target="Interpretation"/>
  </state>

  <state id="Interpretation" initial="Idle">
    <onentry>
      <send event="bot.ability.ready" target="#_parent"/>
    </onentry>

    <!-- Scored sounds are taken here, one at a time; the open speech is
         clear whenever the interpretation is idle. -->
    <state id="Idle">
      <onentry>
        <assign location="open_frames" expr="[]"/>
        <assign location="open_sensed" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="active_source_ids" expr="[]"/>
        <assign location="active_voice_embedding" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="active_participants" expr="[]"/>
        <assign location="utterance" expr="null"/>
        <assign location="stage" expr="null"/>
      </onentry>
      <!-- Speaking's copy of what it said: the bot's own voice, heard
           until it is known. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.efference.json"
                  cond="learnsOwnVoice(_event)" target="DetectingOwnVoice">
        <assign location="utterance" expr="ownUtterance(_event)"/>
      </transition>
      <!-- The bot's own voice arriving as predicted opens no utterance. -->
      <transition event="bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output.json"
                  cond="isPredictedOwnVoice(_event.data)"/>
      <transition event="bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output.json" target="DetectingVoice">
        <assign location="sensed" expr="_event.data"/>
        <foreach array="soundParticipants(sensed)" item="participant">
          <if cond="isNewParticipant(participant)">
            <assign location="active_participants[active_participants.length]" expr="participant"/>
          </if>
        </foreach>
      </transition>
    </state>

    <!-- One busy region: the deferral and the stage failure policy live
         once, not on every stage. -->
    <state id="Working" initial="DetectingVoice">
      <transition event="bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output.json">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.speaking.efference" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.speaking.efference.json"
                  cond="learnsOwnVoice(_event)">
        <event:defer/>
      </transition>
      <transition event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.stage.failed.json"
                  cond="isCurrentStageFailure(_event)" target="Idle">
        <send event="bot.ability.listening.failed" target="#_parent">
          <content expr="_event.data"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A stage child that cannot run. -->
      <transition event="error.*" cond="hasStage()">
        <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
          <content expr="stageErrorFailure(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>
      <!-- A stage child's failure (its <donedata> {message}). -->
      <transition event="done.invoke" cond="isStageChildFailure(_event)">
        <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
          <content expr="childFailure(_event)"/>
        </send>
      </transition>

      <!-- Voice detection on a sound with the window closed. -->
      <state id="DetectingVoice">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'voice_detection'"/>
          <assign location="detection" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="serial" expr="nextSerial()"/>
          <assign location="media_dir" expr="soundMediaDir()"/>
          <send id="voice-detection-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="voice-detection-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="voice_detection" type="scxml" src="../voice_detection/voice_detection.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="sensed.sound.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.media_type)"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.sample_rate_hz)"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.channels)"/>
          <param name="output" expr="soundOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_detection"
                    cond="isApplyData(_event)">
          <assign location="result" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="detection" expr="detectionRecord()"/>
          <if cond="isRenormalized()">
            <assign location="detection.sensed" expr="renormalizedSensed()"/>
          </if>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_detection" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Voice detection child produced a non-ApplyData terminal.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- The routes, in order. -->
        <transition cond="dropsSilence()"
                    target="Idle"/>
        <transition cond="handsOffSilence()"
                    target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion" expr="soundCompletion('detection')"/>
        </transition>
        <transition cond="classifiesSilence()"
                    target="ClassifyingSound"/>
        <transition cond="identifiesDirectly()" target="IdentifyingVoiceDirect"/>
        <!-- VAD Start: open the window with this frame. -->
        <transition cond="isDetected()" target="HearingSpeech">
          <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          <assign location="open_frames" expr="openingFrames()"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- The open-speech window: the next scored sound is fed to voice
           detection. -->
      <state id="HearingSpeech">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="null"/>
          <!-- The frame just heard, streamed when Listening owns no
               decoder. -->
          <assign location="audible" expr="isAudible(detection.sensed)"/>
          <assign location="audible" expr="streamsFrame()"/>
          <if cond="streamsPcmFrame()">
            <assign location="product" expr="frameProduct()"/>
            <assign location="product.participants" expr="active_participants"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.listening.speech.output" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="product"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </onentry>
        <!-- Nor does it join the open one: the person's words stay whole
             and theirs while the bot talks over them. -->
        <transition event="bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output.json"
                    cond="isPredictedOwnVoice(_event.data)"/>
        <transition event="bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.listening.sensitivity.output.json" target="FeedingSpeech">
          <assign location="sensed" expr="_event.data"/>
          <foreach array="soundParticipants(sensed)" item="participant">
            <if cond="isNewParticipant(participant)">
              <assign location="active_participants[active_participants.length]" expr="participant"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Voice detection on a sound with the window open. -->
      <state id="FeedingSpeech">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'voice_detection'"/>
          <assign location="detection" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="serial" expr="nextSerial()"/>
          <assign location="media_dir" expr="soundMediaDir()"/>
          <send id="feeding-speech-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="feeding-speech-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="speech_voice_detection" type="scxml" src="../voice_detection/voice_detection.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="sensed.sound.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.media_type)"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.sample_rate_hz)"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="orNull(sensed.sound.channels)"/>
          <param name="output" expr="soundOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_voice_detection"
                    cond="isApplyData(_event)">
          <assign location="result" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="detection" expr="detectionRecord()"/>
          <if cond="isRenormalized()">
            <assign location="detection.sensed" expr="renormalizedSensed()"/>
          </if>
          <!-- The frame joins the utterance, voiced or not. -->
          <assign location="open_frames" expr="openFramesWithFrame()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_voice_detection" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Voice detection child produced a non-ApplyData terminal.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- Still in voice: the loudest frame is remembered. -->
        <transition cond="isStillVoiced()" target="HearingSpeech">
          <if cond="isFirstLevelledFrame()">
            <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          <elseif cond="isLouderFrame()"/>
            <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          </if>
        </transition>
        <!-- VAD End. -->
        <transition cond="isDetected()" target="SpeechEnded"/>
      </state>

      <!-- After VAD End: the closing frame is streamed, then the utterance
           is joined for diarization or decoding. -->
      <state id="SpeechEnded">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="audible" expr="isAudible(detection.sensed)"/>
          <assign location="audible" expr="streamsFrame()"/>
          <if cond="streamsPcmFrame()">
            <assign location="product" expr="frameProduct()"/>
            <assign location="product.participants" expr="active_participants"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.listening.speech.output" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="product"/>
            </send>
          </if>
          <assign location="stage" expr="openSpeechStage()"/>
          <assign location="open_wav" expr="opensWav()"/>
          <send id="open-speech-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="open-speech-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <transition cond="readsNoUtterance()" target="Idle"/>
        <invoke id="open_speech" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/speech">
          <param name="operation" expr="'append'"/>
          <param name="frames" expr="open_frames"/>
          <param name="output" expr="utteranceOutput()"/>
          <param name="wav" expr="open_wav"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="bot.ability.failed" event:schema="../schemas/bot.ability.failed.json">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="childFailure(_event)"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.open_speech" cond="isUtteranceToDiarize(_event)" target="DiarizingVoice">
          <assign location="utterance" expr="_event.data"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.open_speech" cond="hasAudio(_event)" target="DecodingSpeech">
          <assign location="utterance" expr="_event.data"/>
          <assign location="completion" expr="null"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Non-speech labelling: a labelled sound is not speech. -->
      <state id="ClassifyingSound">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'sound_classification'"/>
          <send id="sound-classification-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="sound-classification-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="sound_classification" type="scxml" src="../sound_classification/sound_classification.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="detection.sensed.sound.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="orNull(detection.sensed.sound.media_type)"/>
          <param name="kind" expr="orNull(detection.sensed.sound.kind)"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.sound_classification"
                    cond="hasAnyLabel(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion" expr="soundCompletion('labelled')"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.sound_classification" cond="isUnlabelledForDecoder(_event)"
                    target="Idle"/>
        <transition event="done.invoke.sound_classification" cond="hasLabels(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion" expr="soundCompletion('detection')"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.sound_classification">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Sound classification child produced invalid output.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Who spoke when in the closed utterance. -->
      <state id="DiarizingVoice">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'voice_diarization'"/>
          <send id="voice-diarization-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="voice-diarization-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="voice_diarization" type="scxml" src="../voice_diarization/voice_diarization.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="utterance.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="utterance.media_type"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="utterance.sample_rate_hz"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="utterance.channels"/>
          <param name="output" expr="diarizedOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_diarization" cond="isDiarizedToIdentify(_event)"
                    target="IdentifyingVoice">
          <assign location="completion" expr="diarizationCompletion()"/>
          <assign location="completion.segments" expr="_event.data.segments"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_diarization" cond="isDiarizedToDecode(_event)"
                    target="Diarized">
          <assign location="completion" expr="diarizationCompletion()"/>
          <assign location="completion.segments" expr="_event.data.segments"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_diarization" cond="hasSegments(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion" expr="diarizationCompletion()"/>
          <assign location="completion.segments" expr="_event.data.segments"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_diarization" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Voice diarization child produced invalid output.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Direct identification of the opening voice span. -->
      <state id="IdentifyingVoiceDirect">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'voice_identification'"/>
          <send id="direct-identification-timer" event="IdentifyingVoiceDirect.after" delayexpr="identifyDelay()"/>
          <assign location="mismatch" expr="'voice identification requires audio/pcm with sample rate and channels.'"/>
          <if cond="cannotIdentifyOpening()">
            <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
              <content expr="openingConversionFailure()"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="direct-identification-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="direct_voice_identification" type="scxml" src="../voice_identification/voice_identification.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="detection.sensed.sound.audio"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="detection.sensed.sound.sample_rate_hz"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="soundChannels(detection.sensed.sound)"/>
          <param name="start_seconds" expr="openingStart()"/>
          <param name="end_seconds" expr="openingEnd()"/>
          <param name="output" expr="voiceOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <!-- No embedding for the opening span, or none in time: the window
             opens with this frame and nobody identified (decision
             D177). -->
        <transition event="done.invoke.direct_voice_identification"
                    cond="hasNoEmbedding(_event)" target="HearingSpeech">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="'no embedding for the opening voice'"/>
          <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          <assign location="open_frames" expr="openingFrames()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="IdentifyingVoiceDirect.after" cond="isIdentifyTimer(_event)" target="HearingSpeech">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="identifyTimedOut(1)"/>
          <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          <assign location="open_frames" expr="openingFrames()"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- The first segment's identity is committed, then the window
             opens with this frame. -->
        <transition event="done.invoke.direct_voice_identification" cond="hasEmbeddings(_event)" target="HearingSpeech">
          <assign location="active_voice_embedding" expr="firstEmbedding(_event)"/>
          <assign location="active_source_ids" expr="activeSourceIds()"/>
          <assign location="open_sensed" expr="detection.sensed"/>
          <assign location="open_frames" expr="openingFrames()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.direct_voice_identification" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Voice identification child produced invalid output.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- One embedding per diarized segment. -->
      <state id="IdentifyingVoice">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'voice_identification'"/>
          <send id="voice-identification-timer" event="IdentifyingVoice.after" delayexpr="identifyDelay()"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="voice-identification-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="voice_identification" type="scxml" src="../voice_identification/voice_identification.scx">
          <param name="segments" expr="completion.segments"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_identification"
                    cond="isEmbeddingCountMismatch(_event)">
          <assign location="mismatch" expr="embeddingCountMismatch(_event)"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="embeddingCountFailure()"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_identification" cond="hasEmbeddings(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion.kind" expr="identifiedKind()"/>
          <assign location="completion.embeddings" expr="_event.data.embeddings"/>
        </transition>
        <!-- Nobody identified in time: identification completes as usual,
             with no voice for any segment (decision D177). -->
        <transition event="IdentifyingVoice.after" cond="isIdentifyTimer(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="identifyTimedOut(completion.segments.length)"/>
          <assign location="completion.kind" expr="identifiedKind()"/>
          <assign location="completion.embeddings" expr="unidentifiedEmbeddings()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.voice_identification" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Voice identification child produced invalid output.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- Speech decoding rewrites the observation into words. -->
      <state id="DecodingSpeech" initial="Detected">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="'speech_decoding'"/>
          <send id="speech-decoding-timer" event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" delayexpr="stageDelay()">
            <content expr="stageTimeout()"/>
          </send>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="speech-decoding-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="speech_decoding" type="scxml" src="../speech_decoding/speech_decoding.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="utterance.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="utterance.media_type"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_decoding" cond="identifiesDecoded(_event)" target="IdentifyingVoice">
          <assign location="completion" expr="decodingCompletion(_event)"/>
          <assign location="completion.segments" expr="voicedSegments()"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_decoding" cond="hasText(_event)" target="HandingOff">
          <assign location="completion" expr="decodingCompletion(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.speech_decoding" cond="isNotChildFailure(_event)">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.stage.failed" target="#_internal">
            <content expr="stageFailure('Speech decoding child produced a non-bytes terminal.')"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- From the window directly, or after diarization. -->
        <state id="Detected"/>
        <state id="Diarized"/>
      </state>

      <!-- The bot's own voice, from speaking's copy of what it said. -->
      <state id="DetectingOwnVoice">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="serial" expr="nextSerial()"/>
          <assign location="media_dir" expr="ownMediaDir()"/>
          <send id="own-voice-detection-timer" event="DetectingOwnVoice.after" delayexpr="stageDelay()"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="own-voice-detection-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="own_voice_detection" type="scxml" src="../voice_detection/voice_detection.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="utterance.audio"/>
          <param name="media_type" expr="utterance.media_type"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="utterance.sample_rate_hz"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="utterance.channels"/>
          <param name="output" expr="soundOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.own_voice_detection" cond="isOwnVoiceLongEnough(_event)" target="IdentifyingOwnVoice">
          <assign location="utterance.voice_detection" expr="_event.data.voice_detection"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.own_voice_detection" cond="isApplyData(_event)" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="'too little of the bot\'s own voice'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.own_voice_detection" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="ownVoiceUndetected(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="DetectingOwnVoice.after" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="'the bot\'s own voice undetected after ' + stage_timeout_ms + ' ms'"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="'the bot\'s own voice could not be detected (' + _event.name + ')'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>
      <state id="IdentifyingOwnVoice">
        <onentry>
          <send id="own-voice-identification-timer" event="IdentifyingOwnVoice.after" delayexpr="identifyDelay()"/>
        </onentry>
        <onexit>
          <cancel sendid="own-voice-identification-timer"/>
        </onexit>
        <invoke id="own_voice_identification" type="scxml" src="../voice_identification/voice_identification.scx">
          <param name="audio" expr="utterance.audio"/>
          <param name="sample_rate_hz" expr="utterance.sample_rate_hz"/>
          <param name="channels" expr="utterance.channels"/>
          <param name="start_seconds" expr="ownVoiceStart()"/>
          <param name="end_seconds" expr="ownVoiceEnd()"/>
          <param name="output" expr="voiceOutput()"/>
        </invoke>
        <transition event="done.invoke.own_voice_identification" cond="hasOneEmbedding(_event)" target="Idle">
          <assign location="own_voice" expr="firstEmbedding(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="done.invoke.own_voice_identification" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="ownVoiceUnidentified(_event)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="IdentifyingOwnVoice.after" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="identifyTimedOut(1)"/>
        </transition>
        <transition event="error.*" target="Idle">
          <log label="interpretation.unidentified" expr="'the bot\'s own voice could not be identified (' + _event.name + ')'"/>
        </transition>
      </state>

      <!-- The one comparison: is enough of this left for a turn? -->
      <state id="HandingOff">
        <onentry>
          <assign location="stage" expr="null"/>
          <assign location="audible" expr="isAudible(completion.sensed)"/>
          <assign location="product" expr="null"/>
        </onentry>
        <transition cond="isInaudible()" target="Idle"/>
        <transition cond="isDecodingWithoutRate()" target="Idle">
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.failed" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="decodingRateFailure()"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- Decoding rewrites this observation: it becomes words. -->
        <transition cond="isDecoding()" target="Idle">
          <assign location="product" expr="decodedProduct()"/>
          <assign location="product.participants" expr="active_participants"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.listening.speech.output" target="#_parent">
            <content expr="product"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
        <!-- One speech product per clipped segment, each in the format of
             the sound it came from. -->
        <transition cond="isSegmented()" target="Idle">
          <assign location="mismatch" expr="isSegmentSourceMismatch()"/>
          <assign location="mismatch" expr="segmentSourceMismatch()"/>
          <assign location="channels" expr="soundChannels(completion.sensed.sound)"/>
          <foreach array="completion.segments" item="product">
            <if cond="isSegmentRateMismatch()">
              <assign location="mismatch" expr="'voice segment audio format does not match its source audio.'"/>
            <elseif cond="isSegmentFormatMismatch()"/>
              <assign location="mismatch" expr="'voice segment audio format does not match its source audio.'"/>
            </if>
          </foreach>
          <if cond="hasMismatch()">
            <send event="bot.ability.listening.failed" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="segmentConversionFailure()"/>
            </send>
          <else/>
            <foreach array="completion.segments" item="segment" index="index">
              <assign location="result" expr="segmentEmbedding()"/>
              <assign location="product" expr="segmentProduct()"/>
              <assign location="product.participants" expr="active_participants"/>
              <send event="bot.ability.listening.speech.output" target="#_parent">
                <content expr="product"/>
              </send>
            </foreach>
          </if>
        </transition>
        <!-- A silence observation: the sound's PCM with its spans. -->
        <transition cond="isPcmSilence()"
                    target="Idle">
          <if cond="hasSampleRate(completion.sensed.sound)">
            <assign location="product" expr="silenceProduct()"/>
            <assign location="product.participants" expr="active_participants"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.listening.speech.output" target="#_parent">
              <content expr="product"/>
            </send>
          <else/>
            <assign location="product" expr="({})"/>
            <assign location="product.event" expr="'environment.sound'"/>
            <assign location="product.data" expr="completion.sensed.sound"/>
            <assign location="product.source" expr="'listening'"/>
            <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
              <param name="stimulus" expr="product"/>
              <param name="participants" expr="active_participants"/>
            </send>
          </if>
        </transition>
        <!-- Labelled non-speech, or a sound that is not PCM: the
             completion's sound, normalized to PCM where detection did so
             (the completion chain's sensed sound is handed off). -->
        <transition target="Idle">
          <assign location="product" expr="({})"/>
          <assign location="product.event" expr="'environment.sound'"/>
          <assign location="product.data" expr="completion.sensed.sound"/>
          <assign location="product.source" expr="'listening'"/>
          <send event="bot.ability.cognition.input" target="#_parent">
            <param name="stimulus" expr="product"/>
            <param name="participants" expr="active_participants"/>
          </send>
        </transition>
      </state>
    </state>
  </state>

  <final id="degraded"/>
</scxml>
